1
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,020
Saeki.

2
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:12,570
Huh?

3
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,260
Sorry, I mistook you for someone else.

4
00:01:36,589 --> 00:01:37,820
Still no good, huh...

5
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:41,000
"My Summer Of You"
(Episode 6)

6
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:52,640
The reason I chose "Sea of Light"
for our pilgrimage

7
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:54,229
is because at the end of the journey,

8
00:03:54,253 --> 00:03:57,003
the protagonist realizes he was
loved by his parents all along.

9
00:03:57,650 --> 00:04:00,040
It reminded me of how I used to be.

10
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:03,069
Hey, when can we go to the beach
from the final scene?

11
00:04:03,070 --> 00:04:05,450
That's the place I want to visit the most.

12
00:04:25,510 --> 00:04:27,350
Another hour, huh...

13
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,600
Attention, passengers.

14
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:46,309
Currently, between
Miyo and Fukioka stations,

15
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:48,080
a fallen tree has blocked the tracks.

16
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,950
Train service has been suspended.

17
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:54,400
Our staff is on-site
assessing the situation,

18
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,020
but it's unclear when service will resume.

19
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:59,959
We sincerely apologize for the delay.

20
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,690
Please consult station
staff for more details.

21
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,160
Hey, kid.

22
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:32,450
Are you a fan of "Sea
of Light" by any chance?

23
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:33,830
Yeah.

24
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,579
I wanted to see the cave from the movie.

25
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:38,340
The cave, huh?

26
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:40,750
You can only go in at low tide.

27
00:05:40,790 --> 00:05:41,790
Huh...

28
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,170
It's probably a no-go today.

29
00:05:46,090 --> 00:05:47,810
Did you come all this way without checking?

30
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:51,019
I looked into it a little bit.

31
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:52,020
I see.

32
00:05:52,021 --> 00:05:53,980
The wind is pretty strong today.

33
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:56,159
It's dangerous.
You better be careful.

34
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:56,770
Got it.

35
00:05:56,771 --> 00:05:58,440
Looks like this is a dead end.

36
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,380
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

37
00:06:24,670 --> 00:06:27,909
I want to go to Moriya Beach.
Is there a bus or something?

38
00:06:27,910 --> 00:06:29,150
Moriya Beach?

39
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:33,310
There's no direct bus. You could
probably get there by transferring,

40
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:35,110
but it's a huge detour.

41
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,829
I see...

42
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:38,690
I'm so sorry for the inconvenience.

43
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:41,310
Thanks.

44
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:09,000
Guchi...

45
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:12,190
(Did you find Saeki?)

46
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:15,030
(I told our homeroom teacher you
went home sick with a stomachache.)

47
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:23,170
Thanks.

48
00:07:23,670 --> 00:07:28,810
But the trains are stopped because of a
fallen tree. I'm stuck at Tatebuki Station.

49
00:07:33,990 --> 00:07:36,129
- Nailed it!
- Tatebuki Station?

50
00:07:36,130 --> 00:07:37,490
He went all the way out there?

51
00:07:38,610 --> 00:07:41,229
It's that thing. They said they were
going on a movie pilgrimage or whatever.

52
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:42,470
Oh, that.

53
00:07:42,530 --> 00:07:43,960
What was it called again?

54
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,469
White Swan something.

55
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:47,049
Never mind that. Call Toda right now.

56
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:48,050
Okay.

57
00:07:54,250 --> 00:07:55,250
Guchi?

58
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:57,060
Wataru, are you okay?

59
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:01,600
There are no buses or taxis.
I'm screwed.

60
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,900
How far is it to the beach?

61
00:08:04,610 --> 00:08:06,020
About ten kilometers.

62
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:08,400
It'd take around two hours on foot.

63
00:08:09,350 --> 00:08:13,800
He told his mom he'd be home by evening.
You're gonna miss him.

64
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:18,250
Huh? Then shouldn't
you just wait at his house?

65
00:08:21,410 --> 00:08:22,410
- Oh, right.
- Yeah.

66
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:23,750
Idiots.

67
00:08:23,990 --> 00:08:25,976
It defeats the purpose if they
don't meet at the sacred spot!

68
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,409
Asada?

69
00:08:27,410 --> 00:08:29,690
Stop hesitating.
Just run there!

70
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:33,490
Hey, Wataru is in the go-home club.

71
00:08:33,590 --> 00:08:34,590
Exactly.

72
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:35,650
Wait...

73
00:08:35,670 --> 00:08:37,050
Start with some stretching.

74
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,970
Stretch your Achilles tendon properly.

75
00:08:41,470 --> 00:08:43,310
Remember to stay hydrated.

76
00:08:43,910 --> 00:08:44,910
Yeah.

77
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:47,380
No need to rush. Just jog at a steady pace.

78
00:08:47,810 --> 00:08:49,570
It's fine to walk up the hills.

79
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:50,860
Yeah.
Okay.

80
00:08:51,431 --> 00:08:55,510
Relax your shoulders and
swing your arms lightly.

81
00:08:58,170 --> 00:08:59,170
Got it.

82
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:03,030
Also, this message will
self-destruct in five seconds...

83
00:09:03,170 --> 00:09:04,210
Okay.

84
00:09:06,890 --> 00:09:07,890
He took off.

85
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:09,630
He sure did.

86
00:09:10,690 --> 00:09:14,190
I'm just showing respect
to those two movie nerds.

87
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:16,340
I know.

88
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:32,820
You can do it, Wataru.

89
00:09:51,650 --> 00:09:55,480
Relax your shoulders.
Swing your arms lightly.

90
00:10:51,970 --> 00:10:52,970
Wataru?

91
00:10:57,990 --> 00:10:59,570
Wataru? Why...

92
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:07,700
Saeki...

93
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:10,290
Clench your teeth.

94
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:15,290
Are you kidding me?

95
00:11:15,736 --> 00:11:17,076
What the hell?

96
00:11:17,170 --> 00:11:18,510
What was up with that letter?

97
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:20,550
Of course I'm pissed!

98
00:11:25,570 --> 00:11:27,680
You've been like this
from the very beginning.

99
00:11:29,470 --> 00:11:32,230
Deciding things on your own,
ending things on your own.

100
00:11:33,790 --> 00:11:35,710
Do my feelings mean
absolutely nothing to you?

101
00:11:37,890 --> 00:11:41,210
Don't just turn people into
memories without asking!

102
00:11:45,450 --> 00:11:47,040
Who cares about a guy like you?

103
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:49,960
Go wherever the hell you want.

104
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,940
I never want to see your face again.

105
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:13,000
I thought...

106
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,030
I'd never see you again...

107
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:35,670
I'm sorry.

108
00:12:38,210 --> 00:12:42,970
I thought this was the only way
I could give up on you.

109
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,320
But over this summer,

110
00:12:51,110 --> 00:12:53,620
as we got closer and closer,

111
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:57,150
giving up became impossible.

112
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:01,770
Instead, all I could think about was
how much I still like you.

113
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:06,700
I'm truly hopeless.

114
00:13:11,010 --> 00:13:14,410
You really are hopeless.

115
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,380
None of that matters right now.

116
00:13:23,350 --> 00:13:25,230
What are your true feelings?

117
00:13:34,310 --> 00:13:36,700
Saying I didn't expect anything
was a lie.

118
00:13:41,410 --> 00:13:43,710
The truth is, I never wanted
to turn you into a memory.

119
00:13:46,910 --> 00:13:48,120
I want to hear your voice.

120
00:13:49,690 --> 00:13:50,690
I want to see you.

121
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,120
I want to touch you.

122
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,330
I want to stay by your side.

123
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:04,770
I want you to look at me.

124
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,450
Finally, some honesty.

125
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:25,030
Seriously.

126
00:14:25,690 --> 00:14:27,960
You haven't changed where it counts.

127
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:33,790
Besides,

128
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:39,169
making me fall for you
and then just disappearing...

129
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:40,380
I won't allow it.

130
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,210
Are you joking?

131
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,220
Who would joke about something like this?

132
00:14:48,690 --> 00:14:49,550
But how is that possible...
Of course it is.

133
00:14:55,550 --> 00:14:57,240
Have I ever lied to you?

134
00:15:01,970 --> 00:15:03,070
No...

135
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:54,930
I never expected to finish our pilgrimage
in such an unexpected way.

136
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:57,490
No kidding.

137
00:16:00,590 --> 00:16:01,590
Someday,

138
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:03,790
you have to come with
me to my sacred spot, too.

139
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:05,710
Yeah.

140
00:16:12,470 --> 00:16:13,529
Ouch.

141
00:16:13,530 --> 00:16:14,649
That hurts.

142
00:16:14,650 --> 00:16:16,560
Ah, that looks painful.

143
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,640
It really hurts.

144
00:16:21,470 --> 00:16:22,470
Sorry about that.

145
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:25,060
I didn't know how to hold back.

146
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:26,870
I think I punched you too hard.

147
00:16:30,110 --> 00:16:31,110
Yeah.

148
00:16:31,470 --> 00:16:32,950
It hurts like crazy.

149
00:16:38,450 --> 00:16:40,370
By the way,
I'm still mad at you.

150
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:44,039
Do you have any idea
how many times I called?

151
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,590
Or how many times I had
to beg Teacher Yamada?

152
00:16:48,030 --> 00:16:50,590
Disappearing out of nowhere.
Are you a spy or something?

153
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,030
I'm really sorry.

154
00:16:55,190 --> 00:16:56,190
But,

155
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,640
how did you know I was here?

156
00:17:03,570 --> 00:17:04,810
I read your letter.

157
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:10,380
I figured this place must be
really important to you.

158
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:13,470
So,

159
00:17:14,070 --> 00:17:18,080
even if I didn't find you here, I was
determined to track you down eventually.

160
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,290
And beat the crap out of you.

161
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:27,130
Wataru.

162
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,670
Give me your hands.

163
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:42,310
Sorry for making you do
something you're not used to.

164
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:47,560
I like you, Wataru.

165
00:17:49,310 --> 00:17:51,280
Why are you saying it
again all of a sudden?

166
00:17:52,370 --> 00:17:54,380
Earlier, I said I wanted to give up on you.

167
00:17:55,030 --> 00:17:59,510
But as long as I'm with you,
I know I'll keep liking you.

168
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,750
Whether it's now or in the future.

169
00:18:06,750 --> 00:18:10,580
I could never bear to see
you with someone else.

170
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:15,009
But if things stayed the way they were,

171
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:16,930
I'd only be a burden to you.

172
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:21,880
That's why I felt I had to leave, go
somewhere far away where I couldn't see you.

173
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,530
But I...

174
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:28,870
failed to see how you truly felt.

175
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,450
Thank you for coming to see me.

176
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:46,620
Yeah...

177
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,400
We should probably head back.

178
00:18:57,970 --> 00:18:59,050
Wait.

179
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:09,040
This is far enough.

180
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Okay.

181
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:13,660
I actually want to stay
with you a little longer.

182
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:15,170
But I really have to go back.

183
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:16,550
Makes sense.

184
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:20,899
By the way, Wataru, is it
okay that you skipped class?

185
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:23,010
Don't bring that up.

186
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:24,460
Anyway,

187
00:20:24,484 --> 00:20:27,004
I already used a stomachache as an excuse.
Don't worry about it.

188
00:20:27,350 --> 00:20:28,560
Take care of yourself, then.

189
00:20:29,470 --> 00:20:30,470
Yeah.

190
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:37,650
When can we see each other next?

191
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:42,380
I'll be back during summer vacation.

192
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:44,360
Okay.

193
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:49,430
I'll get a part-time job
and save up to visit you, too.

194
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:52,310
Just don't run off to
Niagara Falls before then.

195
00:20:52,710 --> 00:20:53,710
Yeah.

196
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,230
I won't.

197
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:02,020
Saeki?

198
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:03,260
What's wrong?

199
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,340
It's nothing.

200
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:06,980
It's just...

201
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:25,280
Wataru.

202
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:29,540
Just let me hold you like this.

203
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:41,520
I'm so glad I met you, Wataru.

204
00:21:48,820 --> 00:21:52,350
I'm glad I met you too, Saeki.

205
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:08,130
If we were alone,
I'd hold you even tighter.

206
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:12,650
I told you to stop saying
stuff like that out loud.

207
00:22:12,950 --> 00:22:14,979
But when I look at you,
I just can't help it.

208
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:15,710
Why?

209
00:22:15,711 --> 00:22:16,920
Because I like you.

210
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:20,060
Don't say things like that so casually.

211
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:21,580
It drives me crazy.

212
00:22:39,060 --> 00:22:41,570
See you later, then.

213
00:22:45,570 --> 00:22:46,570
Yeah.

214
00:22:47,580 --> 00:22:48,580
See you.

215
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:51,740
Yeah.

216
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:12,520
And so, our pilgrimage came to an end.

217
00:23:16,060 --> 00:23:17,060
But...

218
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:23,000
(3 Years Later, Spring)

219
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:29,610
Welcome back, Saeki.

220
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,180
I'm back, Wataru.

221
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:44,690
Even after the credits roll,

222
00:23:46,670 --> 00:23:48,500
the story continues.

223
00:24:45,540 --> 00:24:47,706
(Next Episode Preview)
- No, no. - What's wrong, Wataru?

224
00:24:47,730 --> 00:24:50,050
I want to hurry up and continue
our story from that summer.

225
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:51,859
I finally get to see you.

226
00:24:51,860 --> 00:24:53,200
Director Zaizen's "Blueprint".

227
00:24:53,220 --> 00:24:53,910
Wanna go see it together?

228
00:24:53,990 --> 00:24:56,819
I never want to see you
make that face again.

229
00:24:56,820 --> 00:24:58,090
I happened to get two tickets.

230
00:24:58,200 --> 00:24:59,200
Wanna go see it together?
